# Built-in Generics Standard
RULE: Use `list[str]`, `dict[str, int]`, `tuple[str, int]` — never `List`, `Dict`, `Tuple` from typing.
WHY: PEP 585; Ruff UP006 enforces; Python 3.13+ standard.
CODEX: .cursor/rules/builtin-generics-standard.mdc (this rule), 06-coding-standards/README.md
DO: `def f(items: list[str]) -> dict[str, int]`; `results: dict[str, list[tuple[str, int]]]`
NEVER: `from typing import List, Dict, Tuple`; `List[str]`, `Dict[str, int]`
